# Day 2: Grup Chat (spec §2, beat plan last-seen-m2.md §3). Raka reads Sekar's phone with Dinda: everyone around
# her knew a piece and kept it. Budget: 4.5k Indonesian words, about 30 minutes, to be retuned after the M1 playtest.

@conversation d2_morning chapter="Hari 2" chapter.en="Day 2" title="Sarapan" title.en="Breakfast" checkpoint
@scene VN bg=bg_sekar_living_day.webp music=bgm_quiet_house.mp3 ambience=amb_kampung_day.mp3 day=2 time=06:50 textbox=nvl

narration
  id: Hari 2. Jumat, jam tujuh kurang sepuluh.
  en: Day 2. Friday, ten to seven.
narration
  id: Gue kebangun di sofa dengan leher pegel dan HP Sekar masih di dada. Layarnya gelap. Pesan tengah malem tadi masih ada di dalemnya, nunggu dibuka lagi. Gue nggak buka.
  en: I wake up on the sofa with a stiff neck and Sekar's phone still on my chest. The screen is dark. The midnight message is still in there, waiting to be opened again. I don't open it.
narration
  id: Dari dapur kedengeran minyak panas dan sendok yang beradu sama wajan. Bau bawang putih. Ada yang masak nasi goreng, kayak hari ini hari biasa.
  en: From the kitchen comes the hiss of hot oil and a spoon scraping a wok. Garlic. Someone is making fried rice, like today is a normal day.

stage
  textbox adv
  show dinda:neutral right transition=slide_left duration=600
  show raka:neutral left

dinda:neutral [right]
  id: Bangun. Nasi goreng dari nasi kemarin. Jangan protes.
  en: Get up. Fried rice from yesterday's rice. No complaints.
raka:neutral [left]
  id: Gue nggak protes.
  en: I'm not complaining.
dinda:neutral
  id: Muka lo protes.
  en: Your face is.

narration
  id: Dia naruh dua piring di meja. Telur ceploknya gosong di pinggir, persis bikinan Sekar. Mungkin itu cara masak telur yang diajarin di rumah ini.
  en: She sets two plates on the table. The fried eggs are burnt at the edges, exactly like Sekar used to make them. Maybe that's just how eggs are cooked in this house.
narration
  id: Pintu kamar di ujung lorong kebuka. Pelan, kayak takut ngebangunin seseorang.
  en: The bedroom door at the end of the hall opens. Slowly, like it's afraid of waking someone.
narration
  id: Bu Wulan keluar dengan mukena yang udah dilepas setengah dan rambut yang disanggul asal. Badannya lebih kecil dari yang gue inget. Tiga hari ternyata bisa ngecilin orang.
  en: Mrs. Wulan comes out with her prayer robe half off and her hair pinned up any old way. She's smaller than I remember. It turns out three days can shrink a person.

dinda:hopeful
  id: Bu...
  en: Mom...
wulan [offstage]
  id: Duduk aja, Nak. Nggak usah berdiri.
  en: Sit, dear. No need to get up.

narration
  id: Dia nggak ngomong apa-apa lagi. Dia ke dapur, dan nggak lama balik bawa satu gelas teh. Ditaruh di depan gue.
  en: She doesn't say anything else. She goes into the kitchen and comes back with a glass of tea. She sets it down in front of me.
narration
  id: Gue nyeruput. Tawar.
  en: I take a sip. No sugar.

wulan [offstage]
  id: Sekar bilang kamu sukanya nggak pake gula. "Kayak orang tua, Bu." Gitu katanya.
  en: Sekar said you take it without sugar. "Like an old man, Mom." That's what she said.
raka:sad
  id: Makasih, Tante.
  en: Thank you, Auntie.
wulan [offstage]
  id: Tante belum kuat ngobrol lama. Tapi Tante mau lihat muka kamu sekali. Biar Tante tahu yang di sini beneran kamu.
  en: I'm not strong enough to talk for long yet. But I wanted to see your face once. So I know it's really you here.

narration
  id: Dia ngusap kepala Dinda sekali, sambil lewat, kayak ngusap kepala anak SD. Terus balik ke kamarnya. Kali ini pintunya nggak ditutup rapat.
  en: She strokes Dinda's hair once on her way past, the way you'd pat a little kid. Then she goes back to her room. This time she leaves the door open a crack.

dinda:crying
  id: Itu pertama kalinya Ibu keluar kamar bukan buat salat.
  en: That's the first time Mom's come out of her room for something other than prayer.
dinda:neutral
  id: ...Makan. Nanti dingin.
  en: ...Eat. It'll get cold.

stage
  sound sfx_notification.mp3

narration
  id: HP Sekar geter di saku gue. Cuma notif grup. Tapi tangan gue langsung dingin lagi, sama kayak tengah malem tadi.
  en: Sekar's phone buzzes in my pocket. Just a group notification. But my hands go cold again, the same as at midnight.
dinda:neutral
  id: Lo kenapa? Muka lo kayak abis lihat setan.
  en: What's wrong with you? You look like you've seen a ghost.

choice TELL_THREAT by=dinda:neutral
  id: "Berhenti nyari. Demi adiknya." Adiknya itu dia.
  en: "Stop looking. For her sister's sake." The sister is her.
? (Tunjukin screenshot-nya.) | (Show her the screenshot.) [if threat_screenshot == true]
  value show
  +trust_dinda 4
? Ceritain pesan tengah malem itu. | Tell her about the midnight message.
  value tell
  +trust_dinda 2
? "Kurang tidur aja." | "Just didn't sleep much."
  value hide
  set hid_threat true

narration [if TELL_THREAT == 'show']
  id: Gue buka galeri dan nyodorin HP-nya. Dinda baca dua kali. Jempolnya berhenti di kata yang sama dua-duanya.
  en: I open the gallery and hand her the phone. Dinda reads it twice. Both times her thumb stops on the same word.
narration [if TELL_THREAT == 'tell']
  id: Gue buka chat nomor asing itu dan nyodorin HP-nya. Dinda baca dua kali. Jempolnya berhenti di kata yang sama dua-duanya.
  en: I open the unknown number's chat and hand her the phone. Dinda reads it twice. Both times her thumb stops on the same word.
dinda:angry [if TELL_THREAT != 'hide']
  id: "Adiknya." Mereka tahu gue ada.
  en: "Her sister." They know I exist.
dinda:neutral [if TELL_THREAT == 'show']
  id: Bagus lo screenshot. Kalau nomornya ngilang, buktinya masih ada.
  en: Good thing you took a screenshot. If the number disappears, we still have proof.
dinda:angry [if TELL_THREAT != 'hide' && THREAT_REPLY == 'threaten']
  id: Terus lo bales "gue cari lo duluan"? Ka. Lo bukan preman. Lo tukang edit audio.
  en: And you replied "I'll find you first"? Ka. You're not a thug. You edit audio.
raka:sad [if TELL_THREAT != 'hide' && THREAT_REPLY == 'threaten']
  id: Jam dua belas malem, gue preman.
  en: At midnight, I'm a thug.
dinda:neutral [if TELL_THREAT != 'hide' && THREAT_REPLY == 'threaten']
  id: Jangan lagi. Kalau ada yang mau dibales, kita bales bareng.
  en: Don't do it again. If something needs answering, we answer it together.
dinda:neutral [if TELL_THREAT != 'hide' && THREAT_REPLY == 'ask']
  id: Lo nanya "siapa ini", dan dia cuma baca. Dia mau kita tahu dia bisa baca.
  en: You asked "who is this", and they just read it. They want us to know they can.
dinda:neutral [if TELL_THREAT != 'hide']
  id: Gue nggak takut, Ka.{w} ...Oke, takut. Tapi gue lebih takut nggak ngapa-ngapain.
  en: I'm not scared, Ka.{w} ...Okay, I am. But I'm more scared of doing nothing.
dinda:neutral [if TELL_THREAT != 'hide']
  id: Satu syarat. Mulai sekarang, apa pun yang masuk ke HP itu, gue ikut lihat.
  en: One condition. From now on, whatever comes into that phone, I see it too.
raka:determined [if TELL_THREAT != 'hide']
  id: Deal.
  en: Deal.

narration [if TELL_THREAT == 'hide']
  id: Gue masukin HP-nya lagi ke saku. Dia udah kehilangan kakaknya tiga hari. Dia nggak perlu tahu ada orang yang nyebut dia sebagai ancaman.
  en: I put the phone back in my pocket. She's been without her sister for three days. She doesn't need to know someone is using her as a threat.
dinda:neutral [if TELL_THREAT == 'hide']
  id: Ya udah. Nanti malem tidur yang bener. Lo kayak zombie.
  en: Fine. Sleep properly tonight. You look like a zombie.
narration [if TELL_THREAT == 'hide']
  id: Bohong pertama ke Dinda. Gampang banget. Justru itu yang bikin nggak enak.
  en: My first lie to Dinda. It was easy. That's exactly what feels wrong about it.

dinda:hopeful
  id: Grup pendengarnya. Sekarang?
  en: The listener group. Now?
raka:determined
  id: Sekarang.
  en: Now.

