narration
  id: Senin, jam delapan empat puluh. Bima ngirim sesuatu, terus dihapus. Semenit kemudian Sekar bales "ok". Dua puluh menit kemudian dia pamit ke Dinda. Katanya dijemput.
  en: Monday, eight forty. Bima sent something, then deleted it. A minute later Sekar replied "ok". Twenty minutes later she said goodbye to Dinda. She said someone was picking her up.
narration
  id: Jam sebelas malem, Bima nanya "udah sampe?". Orang yang nggak tahu dia pergi ke mana nggak bakal nanya "udah sampe".
  en: At eleven that night, Bima asked "did you get there?". Someone who didn't know where she was going wouldn't ask that.
narration
  id: "Bima bilang ke polisi, Senin dia lembur di kantor sampai pagi," kata Dinda. Suaranya datar. Terlalu datar.
  en: "Bima told the police he was working late at the office Monday, until morning," Dinda says. Her voice is flat. Too flat.

-> d2_podcast


@conversation d2_podcast chapter="Hari 2" chapter.en="Day 2" title="Draf Episode 12" title.en="The Episode 12 Draft"
@scene VN bg=bg_sekar_room_day.webp music=bgm_unsent.mp3 day=2 time=14:20

stage
  show raka:neutral left
  show dinda:neutral right

narration
  id: Siang. Kamar Sekar lagi, dengan gorden yang sekarang gue buka. Laptopnya udah dicas dari pagi. Nggak dikunci. Sekar nggak pernah ngunci laptop, katanya "nggak ada yang mau nyolong laptop seberat batako".
  en: Afternoon. Sekar's room again, with the curtains open now. Her laptop has been charging since morning. It isn't locked. Sekar never locked her laptop, she said "nobody's going to steal a laptop that weighs as much as a brick".
narration
  id: Browser-nya masih kebuka di halaman masuk situs hosting podcast-nya. "Suara Pesisir, Dasbor Kreator." Email-nya udah keisi. Sandinya kosong.
  en: The browser is still open on the login page of her podcast host. "Suara Pesisir, Creator Dashboard." The email is filled in. The password is empty.
narration
  id: Di bawah kolom sandi ada tulisan kecil. "Petunjuk dari pemilik akun:{w} kapal siapa, jam berapa."
  en: Under the password field is a line of small print. "Hint from the account owner:{w} whose boat, what time."

dinda:neutral [right]
  id: Sebulan lalu Kak Sekar ganti semua sandinya. Gue lihat dia nulis-nulis di kertas, terus kertasnya dibakar di wastafel. Gue kira dia lebay.
  en: A month ago Sekar changed all her passwords. I saw her writing on a piece of paper, then she burned it in the sink. I thought she was being dramatic.
raka:neutral [left]
  id: Sandinya selalu jam yang ada ceritanya. Yang ini minta lebih dari angka.
  en: Her passwords are always a time with a story. This one wants more than numbers.

input DASH_PASS by=raka label=dash_pass max_length=24
  id: Masukkan sandi dasbor. Petunjuk: "kapal siapa, jam berapa".
  en: Enter the dashboard password. Hint: "whose boat, what time".

branch
  if DASH_PASS == 'karta0530' || DASH_PASS == 'Karta0530' || DASH_PASS == 'KARTA0530' || DASH_PASS == 'karta05.30' || DASH_PASS == 'Karta05.30' || DASH_PASS == 'pakkarta0530' || DASH_PASS == 'PakKarta0530' || DASH_PASS == 'Pakkarta0530' -> #dash_open
  if DASH_PASS == '0530' || DASH_PASS == '05.30' || DASH_PASS == '05:30' -> #dash_time
  if DASH_PASS == 'karta' || DASH_PASS == 'Karta' || DASH_PASS == 'KARTA' || DASH_PASS == 'pakkarta' || DASH_PASS == 'PakKarta' -> #dash_name

+dash_tries
stage
  sound sfx_wrong_code.mp3
system
  id: Sandi salah
  en: Wrong password
raka:worried [if dash_tries == 1]
  id: Kapal siapa. Jam berapa. Dia nulis petunjuk ini buat dirinya sendiri. Atau buat orang yang tahu ceritanya.
  en: Whose boat. What time. She wrote this hint for herself. Or for someone who knows the story.
dinda:neutral [if dash_tries == 2]
  id: Kemarin lo bilang kodenya jam kapal yang harusnya lo naikin bareng dia. Kapalnya punya siapa?
  en: Yesterday you said the code was the time of the boat you were supposed to take with her. Whose boat was it?
-> #dash_check

stage label=dash_time
  sound sfx_wrong_code.mp3
system
  id: Sandi salah
  en: Wrong password
raka:worried
  id: Jamnya bener, gue yakin. Tapi petunjuknya nanya dua hal. Kapalnya punya siapa.
  en: The time's right, I'm sure of it. But the hint asks for two things. Whose boat it was.
+dash_tries
-> #dash_check

stage label=dash_name
  sound sfx_wrong_code.mp3
system
  id: Sandi salah
  en: Wrong password
raka:worried
  id: Namanya doang nggak cukup. Sekar nggak pernah lupa jamnya.
  en: The name alone isn't enough. Sekar never leaves out the time.
+dash_tries
-> #dash_check

branch label=dash_check
  if dash_tries >= 3 -> #dash_remember
  -> #dash_pass

narration label=dash_remember
  id: Kapalnya Pak Karta. Berangkat jam setengah enam. Hari itu kapalnya berangkat tepat waktu.{w} Gue yang nggak dateng.
  en: Pak Karta's boat. It left at five thirty. That day the boat left right on time.{w} I'm the one who didn't show.
narration
  id: Gue ngetik pelan, huruf kecil semua, kayak cara dia ngechat. k, a, r, t, a, nol, lima, tiga, nol.
  en: I type it slowly, all lower case, the way she texts. k, a, r, t, a, zero, five, three, zero.
-> #dash_open

stage label=dash_open
  sound sfx_unlock.mp3
system
  id: Masuk
  en: Signed in
dinda:smile [if dash_tries == 0]
  id: Sekali coba lagi. Lo hafal isi kepala dia, sumpah.
  en: First try again. You know the inside of her head, I swear.
dinda:hopeful [if dash_tries > 0]
  id: Masuk! Kapal Pak Karta, ya?
  en: We're in! Pak Karta's boat, right?

narration
  id: Dasbornya sederhana. Sebelas episode, semuanya tayang. Paling atas, satu baris abu-abu. "Episode 12: Siapa yang Punya Laut? Draf. Terakhir diubah Minggu, 23.48."
  en: The dashboard is simple. Eleven episodes, all published. At the top, one grey row. "Episode 12: Who Owns the Sea? Draft. Last edited Sunday, 11:48 PM."
narration
  id: Ada tiga file. "intro_ep12.wav, 0:41." Di bawahnya, dua baris merah. "seg2_narsum.wav, unggahan gagal." "seg3_dokumen.pdf, unggahan gagal."
  en: There are three files. "intro_ep12.wav, 0:41." Under it, two red rows. "seg2_source.wav, upload failed." "seg3_documents.pdf, upload failed."
narration
  id: Catatan episodenya cuma dua baris, diketik buru-buru. "SEG 2: narsum dari dalam. SAMARKAN SUARANYA. jangan sebut kantornya." "SEG 3: dua dokumen. yg asli vs yg diajukan. bandingin hal. 37."
  en: The show notes are just two lines, typed in a hurry. "SEG 2: inside source. DISGUISE THE VOICE. don't name the office." "SEG 3: two documents. the real one vs the one they filed. compare p. 37."

raka:worried
  id: Gagal. Bukan dihapus. Gagal keunggah.
  en: Failed. Not deleted. They failed to upload.
dinda:neutral
  id: Kuotanya habis. Sama kayak pesan buat lo.
  en: Out of data. Same as the message to you.

narration
  id: Gue pasang headphone dan nyolok kabelnya ke laptop. Kebiasaan lama. Satu sisi buat gue, satu sisi gue sodorin ke Dinda.
  en: I put on my headphones and plug them into the laptop. Old habit. One side for me, the other I hold out to Dinda.

stage
  music none fade=1.5s

sekar voice=vo_d2_ep12_01.mp3 [offstage]
  id: Halo, pendengar Suara Pesisir. Ini episode dua belas. Kalau kalian lagi dengerin ini, berarti gue akhirnya berani mencet tombol tayang.
  en: Hi, Suara Pesisir listeners. This is episode twelve. If you're hearing this, it means I finally worked up the nerve to press publish.
  delivery: quieter than her usual intro, close to the mic, late at night, a nervous smile
sekar voice=vo_d2_ep12_02.mp3 [offstage]
  id: Tiga bulan lalu, ada patok bambu baru di laut depan Muara Angke. Nggak ada papan, nggak ada sosialisasi. Nelayan cuma dikasih tahu satu hal. Jangan lewat sini lagi.
  en: Three months ago, new bamboo stakes went up in the sea off Muara Angke. No sign, no public meeting. The fishermen were told one thing. Don't go through here anymore.
  delivery: steady storytelling, a little anger held under it
sekar voice=vo_d2_ep12_03.mp3 [offstage]
  id: Gue nanya ke semua orang, ini punya siapa. Jawabannya selalu sama. "Ada izinnya, Mbak." Jadi gue cari izinnya. Dan gue nemu sesuatu yang nggak seharusnya ada.
  en: I asked everyone whose they were. The answer was always the same. "There's a permit, miss." So I went looking for the permit. And I found something that shouldn't exist.
  delivery: building, then slowing down on the last sentence
sekar voice=vo_d2_ep12_04.mp3 [offstage]
  id: Episode ini bukan soal siapa yang salah. Ini soal satu pertanyaan yang gampang banget. Siapa yang punya laut?
  en: This episode isn't about who's to blame. It's about one very simple question. Who owns the sea?
  delivery: soft and certain, then the question asked plainly, like a title
set
  clue ep12_draft

narration
  id: Filenya habis di situ. Empat puluh satu detik.
  en: The file ends there. Forty-one seconds.
narration
  id: Gue puter sekali lagi, kali ini pake kuping kerja. Napasnya dipotong rapi. Nggak ada "eee". Noise kipas angin di belakang dibersihin tanpa bikin suaranya kedengeran kayak di dalem kaleng.
  en: I play it again, this time with my work ears. The breaths are trimmed neatly. No "umm"s. The fan noise in the background is cleaned up without making her sound like she's inside a tin can.
raka:sad
  id: Dia ngedit sendiri. Lo belajar, Kar.
  en: She edited it herself. You learned, Kar.
dinda:crying
  id: Itu suara dia. Kayak dia lagi duduk di sini.
  en: That's her voice. Like she's sitting right here.

# The fourth of Sekar's unsent voice notes (beat plan last-seen-m4.md §6), optional and remembered across runs.
narration
  id: Dinda ke dapur ngambil minum. Gue scroll dasbornya ke bawah. Di bawah sebelas episode ada satu folder lagi. "Tidak terdaftar. 1 file." Namanya cuma angka. "0612.m4a." Diunggah setahun lalu, hari Sabtu.
  en: Dinda goes to the kitchen for water. I scroll down the dashboard. Under the eleven episodes is one more folder. "Unlisted. 1 file." Its name is just a number. "0612.m4a." Uploaded a year ago, on a Saturday.
narration
  id: Enam dua belas. Jam pesan "ok" itu.
  en: Six twelve. The time of that "ok".

choice PLAY_0612 by=raka:sad silent
  id: Puter?
  en: Play it?
? Puter. | Play it.
  value play
? Tutup foldernya. | Close the folder.
  value close

sekar voice=vo_unsent_04_01.mp3 [offstage] [if PLAY_0612 == 'play']
  id: Jam enam lewat dua belas. Kapalnya Pak Karta udah jalan. Gue masih di dermaga kayak orang bego, megangin dua gelas kopi.
  en: Six twelve. Pak Karta's boat has gone. I'm still on the pier like an idiot, holding two cups of coffee.
  delivery: early morning, wind on the mic, trying to sound light and failing
sekar voice=vo_unsent_04_02.mp3 [offstage] [if PLAY_0612 == 'play']
  id: Gue nggak bakal ngirim ini. Gue cuma pengen ada yang inget kalau gue nunggu. Udah. Gue kirim "ok" aja.
  en: I'm not going to send this. I just want something to remember that I waited. That's it. I'll just send "ok".
  delivery: quieter, a small breath, then making up her mind
set [if PLAY_0612 == 'play']
  set heard_unsent_04 true
  remember heard_unsent_04
  clue pier_wait
raka:sad [if PLAY_0612 == 'play']
  id: Dua gelas. Satu buat gue.
  en: Two cups. One for me.
narration [if PLAY_0612 == 'close']
  id: Gue nutup foldernya sebelum Dinda balik. Ada hal-hal yang dia rekam bukan buat siapa-siapa.
  en: I close the folder before Dinda comes back. Some things she recorded weren't meant for anyone.

stage
  music bgm_unease.mp3 fade=2s

dinda:neutral
  id: "Narsum dari dalam." Dalam apa?
  en: "Inside source." Inside what?
raka:neutral
  id: Dalam perusahaan yang punya patok. Atau dalam kantor yang ngasih izinnya.
  en: Inside the company that owns the stakes. Or inside the office that gave them the permit.
raka:determined
  id: Tasya pasti tahu siapa narsumnya. Dia co-host-nya. Gue telepon dia sekarang. Pake HP gue sendiri.
  en: Tasya must know who the source is. She's the co-host. I'm calling her now. From my own phone.

-> d2_tasya_call


@conversation d2_tasya_call chapter="Hari 2" chapter.en="Day 2" title="Telepon Tasya" title.en="Calling Tasya"
@scene CALL channel=thread_tasya day=2 time=15:05 bg=bg_sekar_room_day.webp music=bgm_tense_call.mp3 stay="Belum. Dia tahu sesuatu, dan ini mungkin satu-satunya kesempatan sebelum dia blokir nomor gue." stay.en="Not yet. She knows something, and this might be my only chance before she blocks my number."

tasya voice=vo_d2_tasya_01.mp3
  id: Halo? Siapa nih? Kalau dari media, sori ya, no comment.
  en: Hello? Who's this? If you're press, sorry, no comment.
  delivery: bright but guarded, a busy cafe behind her
player
  id: Gue Raka. Temennya Sekar.
  en: It's Raka. Sekar's friend.
tasya voice=vo_d2_tasya_02.mp3
  id: Raka... Raka yang ngedit itu? Serius? Sekar ngomongin lo terus, literally tiap abis rekaman.
  en: Raka... Raka the editor? The Raka? Oh my god. Sekar talked about you all the time, literally after every recording.
  delivery: surprised, a little too chatty, covering nerves
tasya voice=vo_d2_tasya_03.mp3
  id: Sori. Gimana Dinda? Gue pengen ke rumah, tapi gue nggak tahu gue masih diterima atau nggak.
  en: Sorry. How's Dinda? I want to come by, but I don't know if I'm still welcome.
  delivery: the cheer drops, guilty underneath

choice TASYA_OPEN by=tasya
  id: Apa yang lo bilang?
  en: What do you say?
? "Dinda butuh temen-temen Sekar sekarang." | "Dinda needs Sekar's friends right now."
  value warm
  +trust_tasya 2
? "Gue udah baca chat lo sama Sekar." | "I've read your chat with Sekar."
  value blunt

tasya voice=vo_d2_tasya_04.mp3 [if TASYA_OPEN == 'warm']
  id: Iya. Iya, nanti gue ke sana. Promise.
  en: Yeah. Yeah, I'll come by. Promise.
  delivery: relieved, a little teary
tasya voice=vo_d2_tasya_05.mp3 [if TASYA_OPEN == 'blunt']
  id: Lo... apa? Itu chat pribadi, Ka. Lo nggak berhak baca.
  en: You... what? That's private, Ka. You had no right.
  delivery: sharp, caught off guard
tasya voice=vo_d2_tasya_06.mp3 [if group_alerted == true]
  id: Bentar. Tadi pagi yang bales di grup pake akun Sekar... itu lo? Lo gila ya? Semua orang panik.
  en: Wait. This morning, whoever replied in the group from Sekar's account... that was you? Are you crazy? Everyone's freaking out.
  delivery: alarmed, whispering so the cafe won't hear
tasya voice=vo_d2_tasya_07.mp3
  id: Gue udah bilang ke polisi, gue nggak tahu apa-apa. Terakhir gue ngobrol sama Sekar itu soal jadwal rekaman. That's it.
  en: I already told the police, I don't know anything. The last time I talked to Sekar it was about the recording schedule. That's it.
  delivery: defensive, rehearsed, too quick

evidence TASYA_PROOF by=tasya label=ask_tasya
  id: Tasya bohong. Tunjukkan buktinya.
  en: Tasya is lying. Show the proof.
? tasya_warning
  +trust_tasya 5
  -> #warning
? sekar_notebook
  -trust_tasya 3
  -> #notebook
? [fallback]
  -trust_tasya 1
  -> #nothing

player label=warning
  id: "Mereka nelpon gue. Lo beneran mau publish?" Senin lalu, seminggu sebelum dia hilang. Siapa "mereka", Tas?
  en: "They called me. Are you really going to publish?" Last Monday, a week before she vanished. Who's "they", Tas?
tasya voice=vo_d2_tasya_08.mp3
  id: ...Lo nggak ngerti.
  en: ...You don't understand.
  delivery: a long breath first, very quiet
tasya voice=vo_d2_tasya_09.mp3
  id: Ada orang PR. Dari perusahaan yang nawarin sponsor itu. Dia nelpon gue malem-malem. Ramah banget. Terlalu ramah.
  en: There was a PR guy. From the company that offered the sponsorship. He called me late at night. So friendly. Too friendly.
  delivery: low and careful, like saying it out loud for the first time
tasya voice=vo_d2_tasya_10.mp3
  id: Katanya Sekar "salah paham soal proyeknya". Kalau gue bisa bikin dia nggak publish, sponsornya tetep jalan. Buat gue aja.
  en: He said Sekar had "misunderstood the project". If I could get her not to publish, the sponsorship would still go ahead. Just for me.
  delivery: ashamed, quoting him with distaste
tasya voice=vo_d2_tasya_11.mp3
  id: Gue nggak setuju! Gue cuma... nanya ke Sekar. Terus dia marah, terus gue nggak bales, karena gue malu.
  en: I didn't say yes! I just... asked Sekar. Then she got angry, and I didn't reply, because I was ashamed.
  delivery: voice cracking, insisting
player
  id: Senin malem. Dia bilang mau ke mana?
  en: Monday night. Did she say where she was going?
tasya voice=vo_d2_tasya_12.mp3
  id: Siangnya dia DM gue di akun podcast. "Malem ini ketemu narsum di dermaga. Doain." Itu juga nggak gue bales.
  en: That afternoon she DMed me on the podcast account. "Meeting a source at the pier tonight. Wish me luck." I didn't answer that either.
  delivery: crying quietly, trying not to
set
  set tasya_admitted true
-> #call_end

player label=notebook
  id: Sekar nulis "jangan percaya T" di buku catatannya.
  en: Sekar wrote "don't trust T" in her notebook.
tasya voice=vo_d2_tasya_13.mp3
  id: Wow. Oke. Jadi sekarang gue tersangkanya? "T" bisa siapa aja, Ka. Tetangga. Tukang parkir. Tante gue.
  en: Wow. Okay. So now I'm the suspect? "T" could be anyone, Ka. A neighbor. The parking guy. My aunt.
  delivery: hurt and angry, talking too fast
tasya voice=vo_d2_tasya_14.mp3
  id: Gue co-host-nya dua tahun. Lo ngilang setahun, terus dateng-dateng nuduh gue?
  en: I've been her co-host for two years. You vanish for a year, then show up out of nowhere and accuse me?
  delivery: cold
tasya voice=vo_d2_tasya_15.mp3
  id: Satu lagi, abis itu gue tutup. Senin siang dia bilang mau ketemu narsum di dermaga. Udah. Cari narsumnya. Jangan cari gue.
  en: One more thing, then I'm hanging up. Monday afternoon she said she was meeting a source at the pier. That's it. Go find the source. Not me.
  delivery: curt, already ending the call
-> #call_end

tasya voice=vo_d2_tasya_16.mp3 label=nothing
  id: Itu apa hubungannya sama gue? Sori, Ka. Gue lagi ada janji. Nanti aja ya. Bye.
  en: What does that have to do with me? Sorry, Ka. I'm meeting someone. Some other time. Bye.
  delivery: impatient, brushing him off, relieved to have an excuse

system label=call_end
  id: Panggilan berakhir
  en: Call ended

-> d2_bima_visit


@conversation d2_bima_visit chapter="Hari 2" chapter.en="Day 2" title="Tamu Malam" title.en="A Night Visitor"
@scene VN bg=bg_sekar_house_gate_night.webp music=bgm_unease.mp3 ambience=amb_room_night.mp3 day=2 time=20:15

narration
  id: Malem. Jam delapan lewat. Lampu jalan di gang ini cuma satu yang nyala, dan itu pun kedip-kedip.
  en: Night. Past eight. Only one streetlight in the alley works, and even that one flickers.
narration [if TASYA_PROOF == 'tasya_warning']
  id: Kalimat Tasya masih muter di kepala gue. "Ketemu narsum di dermaga."
  en: Tasya's words are still going round in my head. "Meeting a source at the pier."
narration
  id: Mobil berhenti di depan pagar. Lampunya nggak dimatiin.
  en: A car stops outside the gate. Its headlights stay on.

stage
  sound sfx_gate.mp3
  show raka:neutral left
  show dinda:neutral center
  show bima:charming right transition=slide_left duration=700

bima:charming [right]
  id: Din. Martabak. Telor spesial, buat Ibu juga.
  en: Din. Martabak. The special egg one, some for your mom too.
dinda:neutral [center]
  id: Makasih, Kak Bima.
  en: Thanks, Bima.
bima:charming
  id: Dan lo pasti Raka. Sekar banyak cerita soal lo.
  en: And you must be Raka. Sekar's told me a lot about you.
raka:neutral [left]
  id: Cerita apa?
  en: Told you what?
bima:charming
  id: Yang bagus-bagus. Kebanyakan.
  en: Good things. Mostly.

narration
  id: Kemeja linen, lengannya digulung. Jam tangannya nangkep cahaya lampu jalan tiap kali dia gerak. Dia nggak masuk pagar. Dia nunggu disuruh masuk, dan nggak ada yang nyuruh.
  en: A linen shirt with the sleeves rolled. His watch catches the streetlight every time he moves. He doesn't come through the gate. He waits to be asked in, and nobody asks.

bima:neutral [if group_alerted == true]
  id: Tadi temen gue bilang grup pendengar heboh. Katanya akun Sekar bales.
  en: A friend told me the listener group went crazy today. Said Sekar's account replied.
raka:neutral [if group_alerted == true]
  id: Temen siapa?
  en: What friend?
bima:irritated [if group_alerted == true]
  id: Temen. Banyak yang dengerin podcast-nya, Ka.
  en: A friend. Lots of people listen to her podcast, Ka.

bima:neutral
  id: Gue to the point aja. HP cadangan Sekar. Dinda bilang nggak ada, tapi...
  en: I'll get to the point. Sekar's spare phone. Dinda says there isn't one, but...
narration
  id: Matanya turun ke saku celana gue. Cuma sedetik.
  en: His eyes drop to my pocket. Just for a second.
bima:charming
  id: Gue kenal orang di Polda. Lebih cepet daripada Polsek. Kasih ke gue, besok pagi udah ada di meja yang bener.
  en: I know someone at the regional police. Faster than the local station. Give it to me, and by tomorrow morning it'll be on the right desk.

narration
  id: Dia ngulurin tangan lewat sela pagar. Telapaknya kebuka. Nunggu.
  en: He reaches through the bars of the gate. His palm is open. Waiting.
narration
  id: "Pesan ini telah dihapus." Senin, jam delapan empat puluh.
  en: "This message was deleted." Monday, eight forty.

choice BIMA_PHONE by=bima:neutral timeout=10s
  id: Tangan Bima masih kebuka di sela pagar.
  en: Bima's hand is still open between the bars.
? "HP-nya kami pegang dulu." | "We're keeping the phone for now."
  value keep
  +trust_dinda 2
? (Kasih HP-nya.) | (Hand over the phone.) [silent]
  value give
? "Senin malem lo di mana, Bim?" | "Where were you Monday night, Bim?"
  value ask
  set bima_on_edge true
? (Diam. Tangan tetap di saku.) | (Say nothing. Keep your hand in your pocket.) [default] [silent]
  value silent

bima:charming [if BIMA_PHONE == 'keep']
  id: Oke. Fair. Lo belum kenal gue.
  en: Okay. Fair. You don't know me yet.
bima:neutral [if BIMA_PHONE == 'keep']
  id: Tapi jangan lama-lama, Ka. Barang kayak gitu bahaya kalau dipegang orang yang nggak ngerti isinya.
  en: But don't hold on to it too long, Ka. Something like that is dangerous in the hands of someone who doesn't understand what's on it.

bima:irritated [if BIMA_PHONE == 'silent']
  id: ...Oke. Gue anggap itu "belum".
  en: ...Okay. I'll take that as "not yet".

narration [if BIMA_PHONE == 'give']
  id: Gue ngeluarin HP-nya. Gue nggak tahu kenapa. Mungkin karena kedengerannya dia tahu mesti ngapain. Gue udah capek.
  en: I take out the phone. I don't know why. Maybe because he talks like someone who knows how to handle things, and I'm tired.
narration [if BIMA_PHONE == 'give']
  id: Ujung jari Bima udah nyentuh casing-nya waktu tangan Dinda nyamber duluan.
  en: Bima's fingertips are already on the case when Dinda's hand snatches it first.
dinda:angry [if BIMA_PHONE == 'give']
  id: Jangan.
  en: Don't.
dinda:angry [if BIMA_PHONE == 'give']
  id: Ka. Lo baru kenal dia lima menit. Ini HP kakak gue.
  en: Ka. You've known him five minutes. This is my sister's phone.
bima:irritated [if BIMA_PHONE == 'give']
  id: Din, aku cuma mau bantu.
  en: Din, I just want to help.
dinda:angry [if BIMA_PHONE == 'give']
  id: Kalau mau bantu, bilang ke polisi Kak Bima ke mana Senin malem.
  en: If you want to help, tell the police where you really were Monday night.
set [if BIMA_PHONE == 'give']
  -trust_dinda 3
  -trust_bima 2

bima:neutral [if BIMA_PHONE == 'ask']
  id: Di kantor. Lembur. Udah gue bilang ke polisi.
  en: At the office. Working late. I already told the police.
raka:neutral [if BIMA_PHONE == 'ask']
  id: Lembur. Terus jam sebelas malem lo nanya ke dia, "udah sampe?"
  en: Working late. And then at eleven at night you ask her "did you get there?"
bima:panicked [if BIMA_PHONE == 'ask']
  id: ...
  en: ...
bima:irritated [if BIMA_PHONE == 'ask']
  id: Lo baca chat gue? Itu privat, Ka. Lo nggak tahu apa-apa soal gue sama Sekar.
  en: You read my messages? That's private, Ka. You don't know anything about me and Sekar.

bima:neutral
  id: Gue balik. Salam buat Ibu.
  en: I'm going. Give your mom my best.

stage
  hide bima transition=fade duration=800

narration
  id: Dia jalan ke mobilnya. Lampu jalan kedip sekali, terus nyala lagi, pas mobilnya mundur.
  en: He walks back to his car. The streetlight flickers once, then comes back on, just as the car reverses.
narration
  id: Di gelap tadi, gue kira mobilnya abu-abu. Kena lampu, warnanya perak.
  en: In the dark, I'd thought the car was grey. Under the light, it's silver.
narration
  id: Mobil perak itu mundur pelan keluar gang, belok, terus hilang.
  en: The silver car backs slowly out of the alley, turns, and is gone.

dinda:neutral
  id: Kenapa lo ngelihatin mobilnya kayak gitu?
  en: Why are you staring at his car like that?
raka:worried
  id: Nggak tahu. Belum tahu.
  en: I don't know. Not yet.

stage
  textbox nvl

narration
  id: Hari kedua. Seseorang nelpon Tasya, dan dia diem. Seseorang jemput Sekar, dan dia bohong. Seseorang motret Sekar di dermaga, dan dia nggak ngomong apa-apa lagi.
  en: Day two. Someone called Tasya, and she kept quiet. Someone picked Sekar up, and he lied. Someone photographed Sekar at the pier, and never said another word.
narration
  id: Semua orang di sekitar dia pegang satu potong. Nggak ada yang mau naruh potongannya di meja.
  en: Everyone around her is holding one piece. No one wants to put their piece on the table.
narration
  id: Besok gue ke dermaga. Nyari kapal yang namanya ketutup ban.
  en: Tomorrow I go to the pier. To find a boat whose name is hidden behind a tire.

-> d3_angke
